<article class="env-lemma" id="0B49">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B49">Lemma <span data-tag="0B49">38.31.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Let $X$ be a scheme over $S$. Let $U \subset S$ be a quasi-compact open. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X \to S$ is proper, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X_ U \to U$ is finite locally free. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists a $U$-admissible blowup $S' \to S$ such that the strict transform of $X$ is finite locally free over $S'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/081R" data-tag="081R">38.31.1</a> we may assume that $X \to S$ is flat and of finite presentation. After replacing $S$ by a $U$-admissible blowup if necessary, we may assume that $U \subset S$ is scheme theoretically dense. Then $f$ is finite by Lemma <a href="/tag/0B48" data-tag="0B48">38.11.4</a>. Hence $f$ is finite locally free by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KB" data-tag="02KB">29.49.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>